# Read by ripgrep (gitignore syntax) and therefore by tools built on it. Not read by git, so everything here stays committed.
#
# docs/plans holds historical plans. Many describe designs that later plans replaced (e.g. 15-26 all reshape the snooker.org budget and refresh),
# and plan prose surfacing in a repo-wide search reads like current truth to an agent. Keeping them out of default search avoids that.
#
# Verified behavior with docs/plans listed here:
#
# | Check                                                   | Plans found? |
# | ------------------------------------------------------- | ------------ |
# | `rg <pattern>` repo-wide                                | No           |
# | `rg --files` repo-wide                                  | No           |
# | `rg <pattern> -g '*.md'` / `-t md` / `-g '!src/**'`     | No           |
# | `rg <pattern> docs/plans`, or rg run inside the folder  | Yes          |
# | `rg <pattern> -g 'docs/**'`                             | Yes          |
# | Claude Code Grep, repo-wide                             | No           |
# | Claude Code Grep with `path: docs/plans`                | Yes          |
# | Claude Code Read of a plan by path                      | Yes          |
# | Claude Code Glob `**/PLAN.md`, repo-wide                | Yes (gap)    |
#
# Gaps:
# - Claude Code's Glob tool ignores this file: it passes `--no-ignore` to ripgrep, which disables .gitignore, .ignore and .rgignore alike.
#   https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/97866 proposes `--no-ignore-vcs` instead, which would make Glob honor this file.
#   Workaround: launch Claude Code with CLAUDE_CODE_GLOB_NO_IGNORE=false, at the cost of Glob also hiding .gitignored files.
#   Glob only lists file names, so the leak is far smaller than with Grep.
# - `grep -r`, `find` and editors' search do not read .ignore.
# - .claudeignore is no alternative: Grep and Glob don't read it (https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/46699).
#
# Docs: https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/blob/master/GUIDE.md#automatic-filtering
#       https://code.claude.com/docs/en/tools-reference
docs/plans/
 